  "notes": "{握|にぎ}る is a godan verb meaning \"to grasp\" or \"to grip.\" It has both literal and figurative uses.\n\nTRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n\nSENSE 1 - PHYSICAL GRASP:\n- ハンドルを{握|にぎ}る: to grip the steering wheel\n- {手|て}を{握|にぎ}る: to hold hands\n- {拳|こぶし}を{握|にぎ}る: to clench one's fist\n\nSENSE 2 - SUSHI:\n- {寿司|すし}を{握|にぎ}る: to make (hand-pressed) sushi\n- {握|にぎ}り{寿司|ずし}: nigiri sushi\n\nSENSE 3 - FIGURATIVE (CONTROL):\n- {権力|けんりょく}を{握|にぎ}る: to hold power\n- {秘密|ひみつ}を{握|にぎ}る: to hold a secret\n- {鍵|かぎ}を{握|にぎ}る: to hold the key (to something)",
